{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLJ6gQqyFzMnbA8qss8f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The two examples in the issue already print correctly in this checkout, so the only change I made is a smaller related fix: it stops LaTeX printing from crashing on one unevaluated expression.\n\n**What I checked.** Both issue examples now give the same output as the pretty printer, with or without `positive=True`:\n- `latex(exp(-x)*log(x))` → `e^{- x} \\log{\\left (x \\right )}`\n- `latex(1/(x + y)/2)` → `\\frac{1}{2 \\left(x + y\\right)}`\n\n**The bug I fixed.** While comparing the two printers on more cases, I found that `latex()` hit infinite recursion on expressions containing an unevaluated `1**-1`, such as `Pow(1, -1, evaluate=False)` or `Mul(x, Pow(1, -1, evaluate=False), evaluate=False)`. The pretty printer shows these as `1/1` and `x/1`. In `sympy/printing/latex.py`, `_print_Mul` now sends these expressions down the fraction branch instead of the shortcut that caused the loop. It also needed `Mul` and `Pow` added to the imports. They now print as `\\frac{1}{1}` and `\\frac{x}{1}`, matching the pretty printer.\n\n**One case still differs.** `Mul(-1, Pow(1, -1, evaluate=False), evaluate=False)` prints as `- 1` in LaTeX but as `-1/1` in the pretty printer. That's because negating the expression evaluates away the unevaluated part. I left it alone to keep the fix small.\n\n**Tests.** `sympy/printing/tests/test_latex.py` gives 104 passed, 3 failed. The same 3 tests fail without my change (`test_latex_symbols_failing`, `test_builtin_without_args_mismatched_names`, `test_issue_8470`), so my edit doesn't cause them. Two of them stop with a `ValueError` about a name. I didn't investigate them further."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":356,"cache_read_input_tokens":32776,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":356},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a83a4e9e-d491-446b-a1b7-66244c975429","uuid":"1d638d6e-fc1e-4170-a3e3-c96ec157b105","timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:59:56.706Z","request_id":"req_011ChLJ6gGf3xbC1c24GUZwu"}
